  "question": {
    "text": "Rate of dehydration of alcohols follows the order:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$2^{\\circ}>1^{\\circ}>\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{OH}>3^{\\circ}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$3^{\\circ}>2^{\\circ}>1^{\\circ}>\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{OH}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$2^{\\circ}>3^{\\circ}>1^{\\circ}>\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{OH}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{OH}>1^{\\circ}>2^{\\circ}>3^{\\circ}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "The order of dehydration among three type of alcohols is $3^{\\circ}>2^{\\circ}>1^{\\circ}>\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{OH}$. This behaviour is related to the relative stabilities of carbocations $\\left(3^{\\circ}>2^{\\circ}>1^{\\circ}\\right)$."
  }
}